}
sub:assertion {
<https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/tree/db966bc45986743c3cde6d87ef6b567099bb3b7b> a prov:Entity, <https://schema.org/SoftwareSourceCode>;
    dc:description "Project snapshot assessed through the frozen evidence pack (sha256 009970e344904cd1546e2f2890cb438667be100be1acd5c62083a4d2cf5dc701), captured 2026-10-31T22:07:43.964Z.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci (fractastical/delphi) at commit db966bc45986743c3cde6d87ef6b567099bb3b7b";
    <https://schema.org/codeRepository> <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasAssessment> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--collaboration-bonus>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--collective-capability>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--decentralized-agency>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--execution-validation>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--problem-significance>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--scientific-impact>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    dc:description "DELPHI addresses an unusually difficult and meaningful problem and has built a real, queryable scientific system with many claims, proofs and data tests. Its strongest weakness under this rubric is not implementation but evidence that decentralization itself adds capability: the pack contains no measured collective-versus-single comparison and no documented outside-team reuse.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on delphisci@db966bc4 (Science Claw rubric): 60/100, bonus 0/10";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Weighted total 60/100 (weights problem-significance 0.2, scientific-impact 0.25, decentralized-agency 0.2, collective-capability 0.25, execution-validation 0.1); collaboration bonus 0/10 scored separately. Comparison multi- vs single-agent found: no. Issue #41 claims two four-arm experiments exist, but the evidence pack includes no measured outputs or result table; issue #61 explicitly acknowledges that the quantitative multi-agent versus single-agent comparison is missing. Top fixes: 1. Run and include one pre-registered four-arm collective-versus-single comparison with quality, time, cost and defect metrics. 2. Secure one documented outside-team reuse of the hosted MCP or a dataset that contributes to that team's result. 3. Re-run a broad executable-claim sample, fix drift, and publish a concise reproducibility pass rate with independent faithfulness review.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.93"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.6"^^xsd:double.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--collaboration-bonus> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    dc:description "No documented reuse by another team is shown. Evidence/repo/COLLABORATIONS.md records invitations, active conversations and 1,522 MCP calls but explicitly says users cannot be identified or confirmed; evidence/captured/forum-feed.json shows zero comments on every listed post, and issue #41 states that observed reuse is zero. Issue #56 is useful external testing by Amit within the named project team in issue #53, not evidence that another team reused the capability in its own result. The Fittest work in evidence/repo/plugins/fittest/README.md is delphisci reusing another team's design, which does not satisfy this bonus in the required direction.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Collaboration bonus of delphisci@db966bc4 by GPT-5.6 Sol: 0/10";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-collaboration-bonus>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/collaboration-bonus";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Convert current invitations and unidentified traffic into a named, reproducible cross-team artifact.", "Get one outside team to use the MCP, dataset, harness or nanopub workflow in its own result and obtain a public citation or confirmation.".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--collective-capability> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    dc:description "The collective plausibly enabled breadth and speed: evidence/captured/git-stats.txt shows 515 commits and 13,622 tracked files in roughly 23 hours, while the parallel slices produced 133 tested claims and a large organism inventory. Yet no measured same-task comparison of collective versus single-agent, isolated-agent or centralized execution is included. Issue #41 says a four-arm harness and two 20-claim experiments exist, but the evidence pack contains no protocol output, scores, costs or comparative result; issue #38 is empty, and issue #61 explicitly lists the missing quantitative comparison as a known weak spot. Therefore the pack supports an anecdotal scale argument, not measurable added capability.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Collective capability of delphisci@db966bc4 by GPT-5.6 Sol: 3/10";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-collective-capability>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/collective-capability";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.3"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Pre-register and run at least one comparison on a scientifically meaningful claim-testing task, not only extraction throughput.", "Publish the actual four-arm harness results claimed in issue #41: same tasks, fixed budget, quality, defect rate, time and cost for single, isolated, centralized and decentralized arms.".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--decentralized-agency> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    dc:description "The work is meaningfully distributed but centrally directed. Evidence/repo/chats/README.md records 22 parent chats and 119 subagent runs, evidence/captured/subagent-sessions.txt shows distinct extraction, assessment and Lean roles, and evidence/repo/BEST_PRACTICES.md enforces blind assessor != builder and multiple providers. But issue #53 assigns named workstreams and deadlines from a central plan, the git shortlog is dominated by Cursor Agent and Joel Dietz (367 and 148 commits in evidence/captured/git-shortlog.txt), production publication remains exclusively human-gated, and all four forum requests in evidence/captured/forum-requests.json are still open with zero comments. This matches the rubric's midpoint: multiple agents and roles, but one planner/integrator decides trajectory and merges.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Decentralized agency of delphisci@db966bc4 by GPT-5.6 Sol: 5/10";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-decentralized-agency>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/decentralized-agency";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.5"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Demonstrate forum requests being accepted and completed by independent agents.", "Document completed cross-agent handoffs and decisions initiated by agents, not only centrally assigned parallel slices.", "Let agents discover, claim, hand off and revise tasks through shared state without issue #53 prescribing owners and trajectory.".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--execution-validation> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    dc:description "This is a functioning, externally reachable system rather than a concept: evidence/repo/mcp/README.md documents the hosted MCP endpoint and query tools, evidence/captured/github-issues.json issue #56 records an independent 100-case MCP test with 93 passes, hosted/local agreement on all 100 cases, 32 ms median hosted latency and six specific defects, and evidence/captured/mcp-morpholib-live.json confirms 109 production audits. Scientific execution is also partially reproducible, but evidence/repo/scripts/exec/runs/latest.json reproduced only 3 of 6 selected data claims while 3 drifted, including 141 mismatches for darwin1859-ch10-12; evidence/captured/nanopub-manifests.txt shows cell-geometry remains test-only, and evidence/repo/mcp/README.md states that no assessments are published to the network. Strong implementation and real checks are shown, but not yet uniformly reproducible or externally validated.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Execution and validation of delphisci@db966bc4 by GPT-5.6 Sol: 7/10";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-execution-validation>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/execution-validation";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.7"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Fix and retest the seven MCP failures in issue #56, including Windows local mode and SPARQL ASK/CONSTRUCT.", "Publish assessment records and reviewed cell-geometry outputs beyond the test registry.", "Run the executable-claim suite broadly and resolve the drift shown in evidence/repo/scripts/exec/runs/latest.json.".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--problem-significance> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    dc:description "The project tackles a genuinely hard and consequential problem: converting broad biological laws into source-traceable, formalizable and empirically testable claims across organisms. The snapshot shows the difficulty rather than merely asserting it: evidence/captured/mcp-overview.json reports 1,702 graph claims, 162 mathematical claims, only 63 theorems, only 2 mathematical claims supported by organism data, and 1,508 claims neither proved nor tested; evidence/captured/mcp-organisms.json further shows 1,036 matched taxa but only 2 with bioelectric coverage. This is an ambitious open scientific-infrastructure problem with clear unresolved scientific content, although the pack does not show that solving the whole claim inventory would directly change a working scientist's decisions.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Problem significance & complexity of delphisci@db966bc4 by GPT-5.6 Sol: 9/10";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-problem-significance>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/problem-significance";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.9"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Prioritize a narrow law family with a stated scientific consequence if confirmed or refuted across organisms.", "Show two or three concrete decisions by working biologists that the graph changes, rather than only the size of the unresolved inventory.".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt--scientific-impact> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    dc:description "Substantial usable outputs exist: evidence/repo/README.md reports 880 production nanopubs, 63 theorems (47 Lean-checked and 16 literature-proved), and 133 claims tested against data; evidence/repo/test-data/claim-tests/SUMMARY.md gives the non-cherry-picked verdict distribution of 78 supports, 25 mixed, 21 refutes and 9 inconclusive, including concrete counter-results such as darwin1859-ch09-03 and thompson1917-ch15-08. The organism layer is also large and queryable, and evidence/captured/mcp-morpholib-live.json identifies 109 production MorphoEval audits with stable trusty IRIs such as https://w3id.org/np/RAtXAz-snj7Cj_FaWUUMcagskmw5GaJa2biZxCtyVyp5c. However, only 66 claims were tested on organisms, 1,508 claims remain neither proved nor tested, issue #37 documents false template-provenance declarations in some production records, and the pack does not establish novelty or independent scientific adoption of the results.";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Scientific/technical impact of delphisci@db966bc4 by GPT-5.6 Sol: 7/10";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0-scientific-impact>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "scienceclaw-rubric/0.1.0/scientific-impact";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.7"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/delphisci-db966bc4--scienceclaw-rubric-0.1.0--gpt>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Move more mathematical claims through organism-level tests; the pack shows only 2 currently supported on organism data.", "Obtain independent expert review of a representative sample of extracted claims, Lean faithfulness and biological test interpretations.", "Remediate and supersede production nanopubs affected by the false template-provenance defect in issue #37.".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-scienceclaw-rubric-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci Science Claw rubric assessor (GPT-5.6 Sol)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol-medium>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol-medium> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol";
    dc:identifier "gpt-5.6-sol-medium"
}
